{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-0122"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Orchard Operations Coordination"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "0122"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :agriculture/tropical-subtropical-fruit-growing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:food-security :rural-employment :agricultural-sustainability]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :orchard-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :audit-ledger]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies [:telemetry :optimization :dmn :bpmn]
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "OrchardOpsAdvisor ⊣ OrchardOperationsGovernor, langgraph-clj StateGraph
 (langgraph.graph, orchardops.operation/build), append-only audit ledger
 (orchardops.store/ledger + append-ledger!, MemStore). Fixes a prior
 deferred-stub gap (same compounding class as other cloud-itonami-isic-*
 siblings before their own fixes): `deps.edn` declared
 `io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph` ONLY under the unused `:dev` alias's
 `:override-deps` with an EMPTY base `:deps` map (override-deps has
 nothing to override when the lib was never in the graph, so
 `langgraph.graph` was never actually resolvable on any real build/run/
 test path); `orchardops.operation`'s own docstring admitted \"NOTE:
 langgraph-clj StateGraph integration is deferred ... Stub\" and `build`
 returned a bare closure over a synchronous `run-operation`, never
 calling `state-graph`/`add-node`/`compile-graph`; and `orchardops.store`
 had no append-only ledger at all for a real commit/hold path to write
 to. `orchardops.advisor` was ALREADY a genuine `defprotocol Advisor` +
 `MockAdvisor` before this fix (unlike most sibling actors' dead
 advisor.cljc stubs) -- it just had no real graph node calling it. Now: a
 genuinely compiled StateGraph (`:intake -> :advise -> :govern -> :decide
 -+-> :commit / :request-approval -> :commit / :hold`) with
 `interrupt-before #{:request-approval}` + in-memory checkpointer for real
 human-in-the-loop resume, folding the UNCHANGED `orchardops.phase` 0->3
 rollout gate into `:decide` exactly as the old synchronous flow
 sequenced it. Four closed-allowlist ops (`:log-orchard-record` /
 `:schedule-field-operation` / `:flag-crop-health-concern` /
 `:order-supplies`), all `:effect :propose` only.
 `:flag-crop-health-concern` (Governor always-escalate) and any
 phase-0/phase-1-forced escalation ALWAYS route to a human grower/orchard-
 manager/agronomist via the compiled graph's `:request-approval` node
 (checkpoint-based resume), proven end-to-end by
 `test/orchardops/operation_graph_test.cljk` exercising commit / hard-hold
 (unregistered orchard, and a HARD violation that pre-empts what would
 otherwise be an always-escalate op) / phase-0-forced-escalate-approve /
 always-escalate-approve / always-escalate-reject / permanent field-
 equipment block / op-not-allowed block through the REAL compiled graph,
 including a falsifiable proof that a custom injected Advisor's own
 (randomly generated, non-hardcoded) proposal `:summary` is what lands in
 the committed ledger fact -- not a graph-internal literal."}
